// Both named imports are used, from cn slots only (`of:`, `involves:`): neither is `ttr/unused-import`.
// `Store` is in both imported packages; the named import picks `hartland.core`'s, ahead of the
// wildcard (no `ttr/ambiguous-reference`) — so removing it as unused would break the model. A third
// import of the same package, `hartland.core.Supplier`, names a concept nothing reads (core declares none):
// it IS `ttr/unused-import` — a used import never covers another of its package (review-120 F12).
package hartland.web
import hartland.core.Party
import hartland.core.Store
import hartland.core.Supplier
import hartland.outlet.*
model cn

def role Shopper { of: Party, event: Visit }
def event Visit  { involves: [Shopper, Store], period: { at: visited_at } }
